; fas9_surfaces_view.scr - facit script of step 9.16, second round (F9.18): what the view and VIEWRES at the save do to the isoline
;   proxy graphics of the spline surfaces. Run it with  python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_surfaces_view.scr
; Two extruded splines (one and several spans) and a plain cylinder are drawn once; the drawing is then saved in each view (ZOOM)
; and with each VIEWRES (circle zoom percent) with nothing else changed: surfaces_view [<change>].
_.SURFACEASSOCIATIVITY
0
_.SURFACEMODELINGMODE
0
_.DELOBJ
0
_.ISOLINES
8
_.SURFU
6
_.SURFV
6
_.SPLINE
0,0,0
10,15,0
20,0,0
30,15,0
40,0,0



_.EXTRUDE
_L

20
_.SPLINE
120,0,0
125,8,0
130,0,0
135,8,0
140,0,0
145,8,0
150,0,0
155,8,0
160,0,0



_.EXTRUDE
_L

20
_.CIRCLE
240,10,0
10
_.EXTRUDE
_L

20
_.ZOOM
_Window
-10,-20
270,60
;SAVE surfaces_view
_.VIEWRES
_Yes
100
;SAVE surfaces_view viewres100
_.VIEWRES
_Yes
300
;SAVE surfaces_view viewres300
_.VIEWRES
_Yes
3000
;SAVE surfaces_view viewres3000
_.VIEWRES
_Yes
10000
;SAVE surfaces_view viewres10000
_.VIEWRES
_Yes
1000
_.ZOOM
_Window
-10,-20
270,60
;SAVE surfaces_view zoom_a
_.ZOOM
_Window
-10,-20
140,40
;SAVE surfaces_view zoom_b
